{
  "id": "05-more-than-her-name",
  "title": "More Than Her Name",
  "tenet": "Humility turns gifts into service",
  "durationMs": 67871,
  "text": "Imagine a girl winning a school prize for a model bridge. She carries it home, proud of what she has built. At the door, her little brother points to a crooked joint. \"That's the bit I held while the glue dried!\" She laughs. Then she remembers the teacher who explained the design, her mother who found the materials, and the friend who helped her start again when it collapsed. The next day, she thanks them. When another pupil struggles with a project, she pulls up a chair.\n\nHumility does not require you to deny the work you did. It asks you to tell the truth about everything you received. Your breath, your opportunities, your teachers, your gifts: none began entirely with you. Thank God for what is good in your life, and let gratitude become service. You can celebrate an achievement without making yourself the centre of every good thing. The bridge can carry more than your name. It can become a way to help someone else cross.\n\nName one person whose help you have overlooked. Thank them. Then use something you have learned to help another person. Let gratitude become service.",
